        "id": 1039103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-25T16:36:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Order is (only if interface creation is possible):\n- AP, STA, P2P, NAN\n- random within\n\nAgree with comment about: \"all\" and \"random\". But that\u0027s a design question. What semantics do we want here?\n\nOne could consider changing the callback API to return a boolean indicating interest from the client (and if client returns true I stop calling others). The problem is the threading model - we\u0027re dispatching on a separate thread so can\u0027t wait for return value.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1620,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1622,
        "endChar": 13
      },
